+
+// Edits made on another device can leave data that no single device wrote.
+// Split lines away from their parent (an older app version, or a line and
+// its parent moved on different devices) are put back with the parent.
+// Transfers whose sides ended up with different amounts (both sides edited
+// at once on different devices) are never changed automatically, since that
+// would silently drop someone's figure: they are reported instead, on every
+// sync until someone fixes them. So are bank transactions that exist twice
+// in one account. An account linked to the bank on both devices keeps only
+// its earliest opening balance, and a later one that doesn't add up is
